# Local API credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Personal uploads and generated runtime data
/runtime-data/
/uploads/
/local-data/

# Personal FIT telemetry. A FIT file carries device serial numbers, GPS traces,
# physiological values and exact timestamps, so it can identify the athlete who
# produced it. Never commit one to this public repository. Both cases are listed
# because ignore matching is case-sensitive on Linux and macOS; mixed case such
# as .Fit is not covered and must not be relied on.
#
# Known limits, recorded rather than left as a trap:
#   - `git add -f` overrides every rule here. This file is a guard against
#     accident, not an access control.
#   - A renamed or double-extension file, such as activity.fit.bak, is not
#     matched by the extension rules.
#   - This blocks DATARA's own future synthetic fixtures too, because no
#     fixture is currently cleared for publication: FIX01-FIX04 in
#     docs/management/source-evidence/fixture-provenance.md all carry
#     unresolved rights and no acquired binary. That is the correct state
#     today. When a fixture is cleared, this rule must be narrowed in the same
#     change that adds the fixture, with the rights decision cited, rather than
#     worked around with git add -f.
*.fit
*.FIT
/demo_file/

# Local editor and operating system files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
